1
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:03,450
Meet Clawd.

2
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,580
It used to live in your terminal.

3
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:08,830
Now it lives right inside the Claude app.

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,390
Just say what you want, in plain words.

5
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,600
Point at a file with the @ sign,

6
00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:19,400
and Claude reads your project before it touches a thing.

7
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:22,810
Not sure yet? Switch to Plan mode.

8
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:26,910
You get a clear plan, and nothing changes until you say go.

9
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:30,250
Every edit shows up as a diff.

10
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:32,420
Click any line, leave a note,

11
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,480
and Claude revises it.

12
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:38,150
Then it checks its own work.

13
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:42,670
It runs your app in the preview, and clicks through it, just like you would.

14
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:45,620
Got more to do? Start another session.

15
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:47,610
They work side by side.

16
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,030
Claude Code.

17
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:54,660
Say it. Plan it. Review it. Ship it.
